From 281a73fb33216d0c086b670076b6912dbc0633d7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 17:47:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] worker store: re-send a receipt whose reply timed
 out instead of latching

One worker.persist with no reply inside the receipt budget (worker_receipt_timeout), or a closed
owner link, latched RuntimeSessionStore.failure for the rest of the process: the next write or
turn-lease refresh raised it from _apply, and refresh_tick interrupted the turn with most of its
300 s authority left (mini 11-12 20:39 PT, bb-dev worker; self-heal defect agent-6ba9ac9880).
The owner resolves an exact resend of the same (execution, sequence, digest) from its receipt
row, so the outcome is unknown but a resend is safe.

- runtime_session_store: is_retryable_owner_error(); a retryable failure keeps the pending entry
  and the next _apply / flush re-sends it under its own sequence (never renumbered), up to
  _RETRYABLE_ATTEMPTS consecutive unknown outcomes, then latches as WorkerPersistenceError.
  Every other failure (owner refusals, lost_receipt, outbox_full) stays sticky. Recovery logs
  WARNING "worker receipt timeout recovered after Ns (op=...)".
- turn_facade_lease.refresh_tick: a retryable owner stall is a missed tick like a SQLite lock;
  it still stops via _stop_on_exhausted_authority when the next tick would land past expiry.
- runtime_session_child.close: finish() still runs when the only failure is resendable.

Tests: tests/agent/test_runtime_session_store_receipt_timeout.py (6 red on dc671254d6).
